    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Currently using the default bindings for mini.comment, but on top of having `gc` to comment a line, I also want to add a bind to use `Ctrl + /` to do the same thing",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Currently using the default bindings for mini.comment, but on top of having <code class=\"notranslate\">gc</code> to comment a line, I also want to add a bind to use <code class=\"notranslate\">Ctrl + /</code> to do the same thing</p>",
    "bodyText": "Currently using the default bindings for mini.comment, but on top of having gc to comment a line, I also want to add a bind to use Ctrl + / to do the same thing",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2024-01-09T19:21:11Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Sorry, 'mini.comment' is not designed for this. But you can use one thing that should work (and I think will work in the foreseeable future).\r\n\r\nCall `setup()` twice with different mappings: one for `gc` and the other for `<C-/>`. As `setup()` only creates mappings and does not delete, this should work as expected. So something like this:\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.comment').setup()\r\nrequire('mini.comment').setup({\r\n  mappings = {\r\n    comment = '<C-/>',\r\n    comment_line = '<C-/><C-/>',\r\n    comment_visual = '<C-/>',\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nNote that I tried that in my terminal emulator and it could not use `<C-/>` per se (although mappings are there). `<M-/>` worked, though.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Sorry, 'mini.comment' is not designed for this. But you can use one thing that should work (and I think will work in the foreseeable future).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Call <code class=\"notranslate\">setup()</code> twice with different mappings: one for <code class=\"notranslate\">gc</code> and the other for <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-/&gt;</code>. As <code class=\"notranslate\">setup()</code> only creates mappings and does not delete, this should work as expected. So something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require('mini.comment').setup()\nrequire('mini.comment').setup({\n  mappings = {\n    comment = '&lt;C-/&gt;',\n    comment_line = '&lt;C-/&gt;&lt;C-/&gt;',\n    comment_visual = '&lt;C-/&gt;',\n  },\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.comment<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>()\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.comment<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">mappings</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">comment</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;C-/&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">comment_line</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;C-/&gt;&lt;C-/&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">comment_visual</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;C-/&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n  },\n})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note that I tried that in my terminal emulator and it could not use <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-/&gt;</code> per se (although mappings are there). <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;M-/&gt;</code> worked, though.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Sorry, 'mini.comment' is not designed for this. But you can use one thing that should work (and I think will work in the foreseeable future).\nCall setup() twice with different mappings: one for gc and the other for <C-/>. As setup() only creates mappings and does not delete, this should work as expected. So something like this:\nrequire('mini.comment').setup()\nrequire('mini.comment').setup({\n  mappings = {\n    comment = '<C-/>',\n    comment_line = '<C-/><C-/>',\n    comment_visual = '<C-/>',\n  },\n})\nNote that I tried that in my terminal emulator and it could not use <C-/> per se (although mappings are there). <M-/> worked, though.",
